## 9. Inclusion and exclusion rules

### 9.1 Include if

The item satisfies at least one of:

- [ ] Mentions Singapore and outdoor workers and heat stress / heat illness.
- [ ] Mentions MOM, WSH Council, or WSH rules in connection with heat.
- [ ] Discusses Singapore outdoor work conditions under hot weather and refers to regulation, enforcement, employer duties, rest breaks, hydration, shade, or acclimatisation.
- [ ] Quotes workers, employers, unions, NGOs, or officials on Singapore heat-work policy.
- [ ] Discusses a Singapore heat incident at an outdoor workplace and links it to policy or employer duty.

### 9.2 Exclude if

The item is only about:

- [ ] General hot weather with no workplace policy connection.
- [ ] Indoor office cooling or air-conditioning.
- [ ] Sports hydration with no workplace policy connection.
- [ ] Non-Singapore heat policy, unless explicitly comparing with Singapore.
- [ ] Heat pumps, appliances, or energy policy.
- [ ] Pure weather forecasts.
- [ ] Tourism or leisure heat advice.
- [ ] Private personal conversations.

### 9.3 Borderline cases

Mark as `borderline` and send to human review if:

- It mentions heat and Singapore but not outdoor work.
- It mentions outdoor work but not policy.
- It mentions policy but is satire or sarcasm.
- It is machine-translated with low confidence.
- It is from an anonymous account making serious non-compliance claims.
- It may be coordinated or astroturfed.

