## 10. Relevance scoring

Assign a relevance score from 0 to 1.

| Score | Definition |
|---|---|
| `0.0` | Not relevant |
| `0.1–0.3` | Weak relevance; general heat or Singapore only |
| `0.4–0.6` | Borderline; outdoor work or heat policy but missing key link |
| `0.7–0.85` | Clearly relevant; discusses Singapore outdoor heat issue and policy implication |
| `0.9–1.0` | Directly discusses the 1 Dec outdoor-worker heat policy or enforcement |

### Required relevance conditions

For automatic inclusion, require at least two of:

1. Singapore context.
2. Outdoor work or relevant sector.
3. Heat stress / heat illness / hot work environment.
4. Policy, regulation, employer duty, enforcement, rest breaks, hydration, shade, acclimatisation.

If only one condition is present, mark as `borderline`.

