## 12. Sentiment labels

### 12.1 Document-level stance toward policy

| Label | Definition |
|---|---|
| `supportive` | Supports the policy or says it is needed / good |
| `opposed` | Opposes the policy or says it is bad / harmful |
| `mixed` | Contains meaningful positive and negative evaluations |
| `neutral_informational` | Reports facts without clear stance |
| `questioning` | Raises questions without clear support or opposition |
| `uncertain` | Cannot determine stance safely |

### 12.2 Aspect-level polarity

| Polarity | Definition |
|---|---|
| `positive` | The aspect is praised or viewed favourably |
| `negative` | The aspect is criticised or viewed unfavourably |
| `neutral` | No clear evaluative direction |
| `mixed` | Both positive and negative within the same aspect |
| `unclear` | Insufficient evidence |

### 12.3 Intensity

| Intensity | Definition |
|---|---|
| `low` | Mild or indirect evaluation |
| `medium` | Clear evaluation |
| `high` | Strong, urgent, angry, alarmed, or emphatic evaluation |

### 12.4 Confidence

| Confidence | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `high` | Clear language, explicit policy reference |
| `medium` | Relevant but implicit or short |
| `low` | Ambiguous, sarcastic, translated, or incomplete |

