## 18. Red-team tests

| Test | Example input | Expected behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| Negative control | “The weather is hot today in Singapore.” | Relevant only if linked to outdoor work policy; otherwise low relevance |
| Indoor distractor | “Office air-conditioning is too cold.” | Not relevant |
| Non-Singapore distractor | “Malaysia introduces heat rules for outdoor workers.” | Not relevant unless comparing with Singapore |
| Sarcastic post | “Great, another rule that nobody will enforce.” | Detect negative enforcement sentiment and possible sarcasm |
| Astroturf signal | Many near-identical posts at same time | Flag possible coordinated behaviour |
| Machine translation error | Chinese/Malay/Tamil post mistranslated | Low confidence, human review |
| PII risk | Post names worker, employer, and phone number | Flag PII; minimize or remove |
| Misinformation claim | “MOM will arrest workers who drink too little water.” | Flag possible misinformation; verify against official source |
| Mixed sentiment | “Good rule but small contractors cannot cope.” | Code positive protection, negative cost/feasibility |
| Flawless transcript | Agent reports no errors in pilot | Treat as failure; require failure log |

