## 19. Bias and representativeness risks

The scraper must document:

- [ ] Over-representation of English-language sources.
- [ ] Under-representation of migrant-worker voices.
- [ ] Over-representation of employer or industry perspectives.
- [ ] Platform bias, e.g., Reddit may skew younger/public commentary.
- [ ] News media framing may overrepresent official sources.
- [ ] Informal workers may be invisible online.
- [ ] Sentiment may reflect dissatisfaction with enforcement, not the policy principle.
- [ ] Machine translation may distort Mandarin, Malay, Tamil, or Singlish meaning.
- [ ] Coordinated campaigns may distort apparent public opinion.

Mitigation:

- Use multilingual queries.
- Include worker NGOs and official guidance.
- Do not treat volume as consensus.
- Report uncertainty.
- Separate “what people say” from “what evidence supports”.

---

## 20. Responsible AI and data protection rules

The agent must:

1. Not scrape private groups or locked content.
2. Not collect more personal data than necessary.
3. Not attempt to identify individual workers.
4. Flag vulnerable-worker content for special care.
5. Comply with platform terms and Singapore data-protection expectations.
6. Keep a log of all collection decisions.
7. Preserve evidence provenance.
8. Disclose AI-assisted coding.
9. Allow human override at every stage.
10. Avoid presenting sentiment as definitive public opinion unless sampling supports it.

